PHP - Looping Through Multidimensional Arrays
To loop through a multidimensional array, use a for 
loop or a 
foreach loop. 

Here, we use a for loop inside another 
for loop to get the elements of the 
$cars array (we still have to point to the two indices):

Example
for ($row = 0; $row < 4; $row++) {
 echo "<p><b>Row number $row</b></p>";
 echo "<ul>";
 for ($col = 0; $col < 3; $col++) {
 echo "<li>".$cars[$row][$col]."</li>";
 }
 echo "</ul>";
}
Try it Yourself »

Here, we use a foreach loop inside another 
foreach loop to get the elements of the 
$cars array.

Here we put the result in an HTML table:

Example
echo "<table>";
echo "<tr><th>Brand</th><th>Stock</th><th>Sold</th></tr>";

foreach ($cars as $row) {
 echo "<tr>";
 foreach ($row as $cell) {
 echo "<td>" . $cell . "</td>";
 }
 echo "</tr>";
}
echo "</table>";
Try it Yourself »

