Use the PHP libxml library to deal with XML errors when loading 
an XML document or string.

The libxml_get_errors() function 
returns an array of error objects, or an empty array if there are no errors.

The following example tries to load an XML string with errors:

Example

<?php
libxml_use_internal_errors(true);
$myXMLData =
"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?> 
<document> 
<user>John Doe</wronguser> 
<email>john@example.com</wrongemail>

</document>"; 

$xml = simplexml_load_string($myXMLData);
if ($xml === false) {

   echo "Failed loading XML: ";
  // iterate over the 
 errors
  foreach(libxml_get_errors() as $error) {
    echo "<br>", $error->message;

   }
} else {
  print_r($xml);
}

?>

